title: Polish Red Autumn events

@candidate
# prose-audit: Grade A — Immersive setup and authored consequences already work; copy-edit only for concision and consistent Lewica voice.
title: Who speaks for the returned Left?
new-page: true
on-arrival: candidate_event_done = 1; news_headline = "The presidential nomination opens every old wound"

= November 2019 — Who speaks for the returned Left?

The presidential election is six months away. SLD controls much of the
organisation, Wiosna claims the obvious national candidate, and Razem refuses
to provide activists for a campaign whose programme it cannot enforce.

- @candidate_biedron
- @candidate_zandberg
- @candidate_primary

@candidate_biedron
title: Nominate Robert Biedroń early
subtitle: The recognisable and historical choice; Spring gains ownership.
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.2; spring_dissent -= 10; spring_strength += 4; media_capacity += 3; razem_dissent += 5; barons_dissent += 2; progressive_credibility += 2; news_headline = "Biedroń becomes the Left's presidential candidate"

Biedroń gives the alliance a modern, European and openly gay national figure.
Razem asks whether it has joined somebody else's campaign; regional SLD
officials ask who will control the lists after it.

- @poland_events_2021_2023.independence_2019: Face the first Independence Day test

@candidate_zandberg
title: Give Adrian Zandberg the campaign
subtitle: A material programme, at the price of SLD and Spring resistance.
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg"; presidential_candidate_base = 3.2; razem_dissent -= 12; razem_strength += 4; labor_credibility += 5; spring_dissent += 8; barons_dissent += 6; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "Zandberg turns the election into a programme fight"

The campaign acquires a sharp position on housing, work and public services.
Biedroń's network does not intend to disappear politely, and SLD barons have
not forgotten who owns the legal vehicle.

- @poland_events_2021_2023.independence_2019: Face the first Independence Day test

@candidate_primary
title: Hold an open primary
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Electorate, ballot rules and preparation determine the field.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources to organise a credible primary.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; primary_active = 1; presidential_candidate = "Undecided"; primary_winner = "Undecided"; news_headline = "The Left opens a presidential primary"
go-to: poland_primary.franchise

@budget_2019
# prose-audit: Grade A — Immersive setup and authored consequences already work; copy-edit only for concision and consistent Lewica voice.
title: The first budget draft
new-page: true
on-arrival: budget_2019_done = 1; annual_budget_year = 2019; next_budget_label = "December 2020"; budget = 0; budget_authority = "Opposition — no state spending authority"; opposition_budget_default = 1; budget_submission_time = time; budget_submission_year = 2019; budget_submission_month = 12; budget_deadline_time = time + 4; budget_deadline_year = 2020; budget_deadline_month = 4; budget_deadline_label = "April 2020"; budget_deadline_active = 1; news_headline = "The first budget draft forces a common opposition line"

= December 2019 — The first budget draft

PiS submits the replacement draft for the 2020 budget. Parliament will vote in
February; December is for reading the bill and preparing evidence. The final
priorities, caucus conference and voting tactic will be chosen once, at the
February parliamentary stage.

- @budget_2019_shadow
- @budget_2019_deal
- @budget_2019_fragments

@budget_2019_shadow
title: Commission one costed briefing before committee work
subtitle: Cost: 1 party resource. Preparation only; February still decides the line and vote.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough capacity to cost and defend a full package.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; budget_2019_preparation = "Costed committee briefing"; health_policy_pressure += 2; household_policy_pressure += 2; labor_credibility += 2; media_capacity += 1; last_policy_stage = "Preparation"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition research staff"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Left costs its February committee brief"

Hospitals, public-sector wages, housing and labour enforcement receive usable
costings. No caucus has yet committed to an amendment or final vote.

- @poland_hub: Carry the evidence into February

@budget_2019_deal
title: Open a committee channel without promising the final vote
subtitle: PiS relations improve; no concession or support is recorded before February.
on-arrival: budget_2019_preparation = "Government committee channel"; household_policy_pressure += 1; pis_relation += 3; ko_relation -= 2; razem_dissent += 2; last_policy_stage = "Exploratory committee talks"; last_policy_authority = "Sejm committee"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Lewica opens budget talks without selling its vote"

PiS receives a meeting, not a majority. Any amendment and every supporting
vote must still survive the February conference and roll call.

- @poland_hub: Carry the channel into February

@budget_2019_fragments
title: Ask every caucus for a written priority before February
subtitle: Cheap and inclusive, but the public sees no common preparation.
on-arrival: budget_2019_preparation = "Separate caucus briefs"; party_unity -= 2; barons_dissent -= 2; spring_dissent -= 2; labor_dissent -= 2; progressives_dissent -= 2; razem_dissent -= 2; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "Each Left caucus files a separate budget brief"

Each faction puts its red line on paper. The February conference must still
turn those briefs into two priorities and one recorded tactic.

- @poland_hub: Carry the briefs into February

@budget_2019_ratification
title: The first caucus ratification
new-page: true
call: poland_normalize
on-arrival: {!
const clampSupport2019 = function(value) {
    return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, value));
};
const commonBase2019 =
    43 + Q.party_unity * 0.36 -
    Math.max(0, Q.budget_promises) * 0.8 -
    Q.budget_breaches * 3;

let barons2019 =
    commonBase2019 - Math.max(0, Q.barons_dissent) * 0.65;
let spring2019 =
    commonBase2019 - Math.max(0, Q.spring_dissent) * 0.65;
let labor2019 =
    commonBase2019 - Math.max(0, Q.labor_dissent) * 0.65;
let progressives2019 =
    commonBase2019 - Math.max(0, Q.progressives_dissent) * 0.65;
let razem2019 =
    commonBase2019 - Math.max(0, Q.razem_dissent) * 0.65;
let pps2019 =
    commonBase2019 - Math.max(0, Q.pps_dissent) * 0.65;

if (Q.budget_2019_package_code == 1) {
    barons2019 += 2;
    spring2019 += 4;
    labor2019 += 12;
    progressives2019 += 7;
    razem2019 += 15;
    pps2019 += 12;
}
if (Q.budget_2019_package_code == 2) {
    barons2019 += 12;
    spring2019 -= 5;
    labor2019 += 4;
    progressives2019 -= 10;
    razem2019 -= 16;
    pps2019 += 2;
}
if (Q.budget_2019_package_code == 3) {
    barons2019 += 3;
    spring2019 += 3;
    progressives2019 += 2;
    pps2019 += 2;
}

barons2019 = clampSupport2019(barons2019);
spring2019 = clampSupport2019(spring2019);
labor2019 = clampSupport2019(labor2019);
progressives2019 = clampSupport2019(progressives2019);
razem2019 = clampSupport2019(razem2019);
pps2019 = clampSupport2019(pps2019);

const caucusVotes2019 = [
    ["barons", barons2019],
    ["spring", spring2019],
    ["labor", labor2019],
    ["progressives", progressives2019],
    ["razem", razem2019],
    ["pps", pps2019]
].filter(function(entry) {
    return Q[entry[0] + "_active"];
});
const totalStrength2019 = caucusVotes2019.reduce(function(total, entry) {
    return total + Q[entry[0] + "_strength"];
}, 0);
const weighted2019 = caucusVotes2019.reduce(function(total, entry) {
    return total + entry[1] * Q[entry[0] + "_strength"];
}, 0);

Q.budget_2019_backing =
    Math.max(
        0,
        Math.min(
            100,
            Math.round(weighted2019 / Math.max(1, totalStrength2019))
        )
    );
Q.budget_2019_vetoes = caucusVotes2019.filter(function(entry) {
    return entry[1] < 35;
}).length;
Q.budget_2019_ratified =
    Q.budget_2019_package_code != 3 &&
    Q.budget_2019_backing >= 55 &&
    Q.budget_2019_vetoes <= 1 ? 1 : 0;
Q.budget_2019_rebels =
    Q.budget_2019_ratified &&
    (Q.budget_2019_backing < 65 || Q.budget_2019_vetoes > 0) ? 1 : 0;

if (Q.budget_2019_ratified && !Q.budget_2019_rebels) {
    Q.party_unity += 5;
    Q.public_trust += 3;
    Q.news_headline = "The returned Left ratifies one opposition line";
} else if (Q.budget_2019_ratified) {
    Q.party_unity += 1;
    Q.public_trust += 1;
    Q.news_headline = "The opposition line passes with named rebels";
} else if (Q.budget_2019_backing >= 40) {
    Q.party_unity -= 5;
    Q.public_trust -= 2;
    Q.news_headline = "The first common fiscal position fails";
} else {
    Q.party_unity -= 9;
    Q.public_trust -= 4;
    Q.news_headline = "The first budget vote opens a factional rupture";
}
!}

= The first fiscal mandate

**[+ budget_2019_package +] receives [+ budget_2019_backing +]% weighted caucus
backing.** Internal vetoes: **[+ budget_2019_vetoes +]**. This is authority for
a voting line, not access to the state treasury.

[? if budget_2019_ratified and not budget_2019_rebels: The parliamentary club
owns one fiscal position. The peace is real precisely because every current had
the power to refuse it. ?]

[? if budget_2019_ratified and budget_2019_rebels: The line passes narrowly.
Senior dissenters reserve the right to reopen it in the next crisis. ?]

[? if not budget_2019_ratified: The alliance reaches the microphones without a
ratified common budget. Every unresolved promise now follows it into 2020. ?]

- @poland_hub: Carry the mandate into February's Sejm vote

