- @poland_foreign_events.us_election_2020: Follow the 3 November result

@budget_2020
# prose-audit: Grade A — Immersive setup and authored consequences already work; copy-edit only for concision and consistent Lewica voice.
title: The pandemic budget
new-page: true
on-arrival: budget_2020_done = 1; annual_budget_year = 2020; budget = 0; budget_authority = "Opposition — no state spending authority"; opposition_budget_default = 1; news_headline = "Every promise arrives at the opposition budget table"
go-to: poland_opposition_budget.start

= December 2020 — The pandemic budget

Hospitals are strained, households have lost income, local governments are
short of money and the abortion ruling has changed the political landscape. The
Left does not control public spending. It must decide what package justifies a
common **no** vote, or deliberately trade that default opposition for named
concessions. Then every caucus will ratify—or break—the line.

- @budget_2020_social
- @budget_2020_local
- @budget_2020_equality
- @budget_2020_deal
- @budget_2020_palace

@budget_2020_social
title: Oppose with a social shield — hospitals, sick pay, wages and housing
subtitle: Strongest labour/Razem proposal; it changes the opposition line, not hospital or household delivery.
on-arrival: opposition_budget_default = 1; budget_package = "Social shield opposition"; budget_package_code = 1; household_policy_pressure += 8; health_policy_pressure += 7; labor_credibility += 6; budget_promises -= 2; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0

The package treats public health as income security as well as hospital
capacity. Local government and equality measures receive less room.

- @budget_ratification: Put the package to the caucuses

@budget_2020_local
title: Oppose with local survival — hospitals, councils and small firms
subtitle: Builds a PSL bridge and an implementation demand; the opposition cannot fund it.
on-arrival: opposition_budget_default = 1; budget_package = "Local survival opposition"; budget_package_code = 2; health_policy_pressure += 6; local_network += 5; psl_relation += 5; barons_dissent -= 2; budget_promises -= 1; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0

The programme can be administered and defended in every county. Feminist and
tenant organisers see another year in which their commitments became optional.

- @budget_ratification: Put the package to the caucuses

@budget_2020_equality
title: Oppose with equality and care
subtitle: Progressive proposal with conservative backlash; no care capacity changes before passage.
on-arrival: opposition_budget_default = 1; budget_package = "Equality and care opposition"; budget_package_code = 3; health_policy_pressure += 4; progressive_credibility += 8; feminist_trust += 8; psl_relation -= 5; president_relation -= 4; budget_promises -= 1; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0

The package turns protest into institutions and services. Labour organisers
support much of it while asking where wage replacement went.

- @budget_ratification: Put the package to the caucuses

@budget_2020_deal
title: Amend selected PiS provisions and vote case by case
subtitle: Requires a government or Palace channel. Negotiated concession now; implementation follows the completed budget.
choose-if: pis_relation >= 14 or government_delivery >= 4 or (trz_inaugurated = 0 and president_relation >= 24)
unavailable-subtitle: No government channel is credible enough for PiS to buy this departure from opposition.
on-arrival: opposition_budget_default = 0; government_favors += 1; budget_package = "Selective PiS deal"; budget_package_code = 4; budget_2020_concession_pending = 1; pis_relation += 8; ko_relation -= 7; household_policy_pressure += 1; budget_breaches += 2; last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession"; last_policy_authority = "PiS cabinet and Sejm majority"; last_policy_implementation = 0

Several useful lines pass. The Left enters 2021 unable to say whether it
possesses a fiscal programme or a list of successful amendments.

- @budget_ratification: Put the package to the caucuses

@budget_2020_palace
title: Coordinate Senate amendments and a veto threat with Trzaskowski
subtitle: Cohabitation pressure only; the threat improves neither hospitals nor households unless PiS concedes.
view-if: trz_inaugurated = 1
on-arrival: opposition_budget_default = 1; budget_package = "Palace–Senate amendment front"; budget_package_code = 5; president_relation += 6; ko_relation += 4; psl_relation += 3; household_policy_pressure += 3; health_policy_pressure += 3; constitutional_restraint += 3; trz_vetoes += 1; trz_cohabitation_temperature += 4; trz_right_fragmentation += 3; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Opposition Senate and President"; last_policy_implementation = 0

The Senate writes the amendments and the President supplies a credible threat
to return the law. PiS must either concede public-health and local-government
funding or call the bluff.

- @budget_ratification: Put the package to the caucuses

@budget_ratification
title: Caucus ratification
new-page: true
call: poland_normalize
on-arrival: {!
const clampSupport = function(value) {
    return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, value));
};
const commonBase =
    43 + Q.party_unity * 0.36 -
    Math.max(0, Q.budget_promises) * 0.8 -
    Q.budget_breaches * 3;

let barons = commonBase - Math.max(0, Q.barons_dissent) * 0.65;
let spring = commonBase - Math.max(0, Q.spring_dissent) * 0.65;
let labor = commonBase - Math.max(0, Q.labor_dissent) * 0.65;
let progressives =
    commonBase - Math.max(0, Q.progressives_dissent) * 0.65;
let razem = commonBase - Math.max(0, Q.razem_dissent) * 0.65;
let pps = commonBase - Math.max(0, Q.pps_dissent) * 0.65;

if (Q.budget_package_code == 1) {
    spring += 3;
    labor += 15;
    progressives += 7;
    razem += 12;
    pps += 12;
}
if (Q.budget_package_code == 2) {
    barons += 12;
    labor += 7;
    progressives -= 5;
    razem += 2;
    pps += 7;
}
if (Q.budget_package_code == 3) {
    barons -= 8;
    spring += 14;
    labor += 4;
    progressives += 16;
    razem += 7;
    pps += 5;
}
if (Q.budget_package_code == 4) {
    barons += 8;
    spring -= 8;
    labor += 5;
    progressives -= 12;
    razem -= 15;
    pps -= 2;
}
if (Q.budget_package_code == 5) {
    barons += 7;
    spring += 8;
    labor += 7;
    progressives += 9;
    razem += 5;
    pps += 7;
}

barons = clampSupport(barons);
spring = clampSupport(spring);
labor = clampSupport(labor);
progressives = clampSupport(progressives);
razem = clampSupport(razem);
pps = clampSupport(pps);

const caucusVotes = [
    ["barons", barons],
    ["spring", spring],
    ["labor", labor],
    ["progressives", progressives],
    ["razem", razem],
    ["pps", pps]
].filter(function(entry) {
    return Q[entry[0] + "_active"];
});
const totalStrength = caucusVotes.reduce(function(total, entry) {
    return total + Q[entry[0] + "_strength"];
}, 0);
const weighted = caucusVotes.reduce(function(total, entry) {
    return total + entry[1] * Q[entry[0] + "_strength"];
}, 0);

Q.budget_backing =
    Math.max(
        0,
        Math.min(100, Math.round(weighted / Math.max(1, totalStrength)))
    );
Q.budget_vetoes = caucusVotes.filter(function(entry) {
    return entry[1] < 35;
}).length;
Q.budget_2020_ratified =
    Q.budget_package_code != 4 &&
    Q.budget_backing >= 55 &&
    Q.budget_vetoes <= 1 ? 1 : 0;
Q.budget_2020_rebels =
    Q.budget_2020_ratified &&
    (Q.budget_backing < 65 || Q.budget_vetoes > 0) ? 1 : 0;

if (Q.budget_2020_ratified && !Q.budget_2020_rebels) {
    Q.party_unity += 8;
    Q.public_trust += 5;
    Q.left_poll += 0.7;
    Q.news_headline = "The Left ratifies a common pandemic opposition";
} else if (Q.budget_2020_ratified) {
    Q.party_unity += 2;
    Q.public_trust += 2;
    Q.left_poll += 0.2;
    Q.news_headline = "The opposition line passes with named Left rebels";
} else if (Q.budget_backing >= 40) {
    Q.party_unity -= 8;
    Q.public_trust -= 4;
    Q.left_poll -= 0.5;
    Q.news_headline = "The common budget fails ratification";
} else {
    Q.party_unity -= 15;
    Q.public_trust -= 7;
    Q.left_poll -= 0.9;
    Q.news_headline = "The fiscal vote becomes an open Left rupture";
}
!}

= The vote

**[+ budget_package +] receives [+ budget_backing +]% weighted caucus backing.**
Internal vetoes: **[+ budget_vetoes +]**. Unfunded promises:
**[+ budget_promises +]**. Recorded fiscal breaches:
**[+ budget_breaches +]**. In this opposition chapter, ratification determines
how Lewica votes and what it demands; the state-budget capacity remains zero.

[? if budget_2020_ratified and not budget_2020_rebels: Every current can
identify a priority in the package. Nobody is entirely satisfied, which for
once is evidence of a common programme rather than failure. ?]

[? if budget_2020_ratified and budget_2020_rebels: The position passes, but
senior rebels announce that this cannot become the next manifesto. The
alliance survives with a dated internal grievance. ?]

[? if not budget_2020_ratified and budget_backing >= 40: The leadership cannot
claim a common fiscal position. A weighted majority is insufficient when a
constituent organisation exercises a red-line veto—or when the chosen strategy
was never a common budget at all. ?]

[? if not budget_2020_ratified and budget_backing < 40: Caucuses no longer
argue about one budget. They argue about which organisation should carry the
Left into the next election. ?]

- @poland_senate.budget_2020: Send the pandemic budget to the Senate

@budget_consequence
go-to: poland_polling

@vaccine
# prose-audit: Grade B — The scene now has a grounded Lewica viewpoint and distinct aftermaths; a later pass need only tighten cadence against the original mod.
title: Vaccination begins
new-page: true
on-arrival: vaccine_event_done = 1; news_headline = "Vaccination begins under conditions of scarcity"

= January 2021 — Vaccination

The first doses reach hospital freezers in a climate already poisoned by
shortages and suspicion. Doctors and nurses ask us to make the public case for
vaccination. Mayors and pharmacists answer that no Warsaw campaign matters if
older and rural patients cannot reach an appointment. Konfederacja is ready to
turn every queue and rumour into a story about coercion.

We do not control the vaccination programme. We can still decide what kind of
trust the Left lends it.

- @vaccine_public
- @vaccine_local
- @vaccine_liberty

@vaccine_public
title: Run a public-health campaign with clinicians and unions
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; vaccination_strategy = "Public-health mobilisation"; health_policy_pressure += 5; public_trust += 4; public_sector_support += 3; covid_anti_system_pressure -= 4; konf_poll += 0.2; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Clinicians and unions lead the vaccination campaign"

Doctors, nurses and union delegates take the microphones while our MPs carry
their case into Parliament. Workplace meetings answer practical questions
more effectively than another ministerial conference. Konfederacja calls the
campaign pressure by another name, but the Left now owns a clear public-health
line—and will be judged by it if supply fails.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@vaccine_local
title: Build access through councils, pharmacies and workplaces
on-arrival: vaccination_strategy = "Local access"; health_policy_pressure += 4; local_network += 3; psl_relation += 2; rural_support += 2; covid_anti_system_pressure -= 2; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Opposition local network"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Local access becomes the vaccination argument"

Lewica councillors begin matching pharmacies, workplaces and volunteer drivers
to the gaps in the state programme. The network is uneven, but in smaller
towns it gives people a number to call and a place they recognise. PSL approves
of the localism; our organisers quietly note that an opposition party is doing
work the government should have arranged.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@vaccine_liberty
title: Concentrate on voluntary consent and oversight
on-arrival: vaccination_strategy = "Consent and oversight"; constitutional_restraint += 3; health_policy_pressure += 1; konf_relation += 2; public_trust -= 1; pandemic_deaths_pressure += 2; covid_anti_system_pressure += 6; konf_braunist_share += 2; konf_mentzenite_share += 2; konf_nationalist_share -= 4; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Left makes consent its vaccination line while Konfederacja recruits around it"

Our lawyers demand informed consent, published contracts and scrutiny of every
emergency measure. The safeguards deserve a hearing. So do clinicians who warn
that hesitation has a cost measured in occupied beds. Konfederacja quotes the
first half of our argument and discards the second, drawing the most suspicious
voters further into its orbit.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@rename
# prose-audit: Grade B — The registration is now an internal-party scene with concrete stakes and authored consequences; retain the legal-state conditionals.
title: SLD becomes Nowa Lewica
new-page: true
on-arrival: rename_event_done = 1; barons_name = "Nowa Lewica organisation"; left_party_name = "Lewica Razem" if razem_merged = 1; left_party_name = "Nowa Lewica" if razem_merged = 0; news_headline = "SLD registers the Nowa Lewica legal name"

= March 2021 — A new name

The registry changes faster than a political culture. SLD disappears from the
paperwork, but its offices, membership lists and loyalties remain. Wiosna
organisers want proof that this is a merger rather than a repainting. SLD
officials still hold many of the keys. Razem watches to see whether the bargain
already made will be honoured.

A new sign is easy. The argument is over who is entitled to hang it. [? if
razem_merged: The common political party remains **Lewica Razem**: changing the
inherited legal vehicle neither reverses the constituent convention nor
removes Razem's lead.?] [? if not razem_merged: Without a constituent merger,
the new name leaves authority divided among Czarzasty's executive, the members,
and the still-separate SLD and Wiosna structures.?]

- @rename_dual
- @rename_members
- @rename_drive
- @rename_machine

@rename_dual
title: Keep the SLD–Wiosna dual structure until congress
on-arrival: merger_leader = "Razem" if razem_merged = 1; merger_leader = "Dual chairs" if razem_merged = 0; left_project = "Nowa Lewica with protected SLD and Wiosna currents"; party_unity += 3; barons_dissent -= 3; spring_dissent -= 3; razem_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Dual structures carry Nowa Lewica to congress"

For now there are two secretariats, two mailing lists and a promise that
congress will settle the rest. SLD and Wiosna organisers keep their familiar
chains of command, which is enough to prevent an immediate walkout. Razem sees
peace purchased by postponement; every disputed nomination now arrives with
two signatures and a future argument attached.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@rename_members
title: Put the constitution to a membership ballot
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: merger_leader = "Membership convention"; resources -= 1; left_project = "Member-ratified Nowa Lewica"; party_unity += 5; progressives_dissent -= 4; labor_dissent -= 3; barons_dissent += 5; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "Members ratify the new party rules"

Ballot papers go to local branches instead of another agreement being written
in Warsaw. Members debate the constitution clause by clause and ratify rules
that neither inherited leadership can call its private settlement. The result
has legitimacy, but it also has losers: veteran officials discover that years
of service no longer guarantee control of the new organisation.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@rename_drive
title: Relaunch the member roll under the new name
subtitle: The drive pays for itself, but local organisers and younger volunteers carry the burden.
on-arrival: resources += 1; left_project = "Membership-driven Nowa Lewica"; local_network += 2; organiser_energy -= 3; young_support += 1; party_unity += 1; barons_dissent += 2; news_headline = "A Nowa Lewica membership drive pays its first bills"

Tables appear outside campuses, factories and municipal offices under a name
that prospective members have not yet learned to pronounce without comment.
Their dues pay the first bills and the new roll weakens the old lists. It also
exhausts the younger organisers asked to recruit for a party whose internal
authority remains unresolved.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@rename_machine
title: Transfer authority to the existing SLD executive
on-arrival: merger_leader = "Włodzimierz Czarzasty"; left_project = "Centralised Nowa Lewica"; barons_strength += 3; barons_dissent -= 6; local_network += 2; spring_dissent += 6; progressives_dissent += 5; razem_dissent += 4; news_headline = "The old executive takes control of the new name"

Czarzasty's executive changes the letterhead, assigns the offices and gives
every regional chair a clear answer about who is in command. The machinery
moves quickly because it is largely the old machinery. Wiosna organisers call
it an annexation; Razem reads it as notice that a new name has preserved the
old centre of power.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@recovery_fund
# prose-audit: Grade A — Each ratification route now has an authored Lewica aftermath naming who owns the votes, safeguards and opposition breach.
title: The EU recovery fund vote
new-page: true
on-arrival: recovery_fund_event_done = 1; news_headline = "PiS needs opposition votes for the recovery fund"

= May 2021 — Recovery fund

Poland needs the EU recovery fund, but Solidarna Polska has taken votes away
from Mateusz Morawiecki's majority. Our MPs can now secure safeguards directly,
force KO and Poland 2050 into one control package, or refuse to rescue PiS and
risk leaving the money to somebody else's arithmetic.

- @recovery_deal
- @recovery_opposition
- @recovery_abstain
- @recovery_palace

@recovery_deal
title: Negotiate safeguards with the government and vote yes
subtitle: The historical gamble.
on-arrival: recovery_fund_strategy = "Negotiated PiS deal"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "Lewica yes votes complete the ratification majority"; pis_relation += 10; ko_relation -= 12; p2050_relation -= 7; relation_pis_psl += 3; rival_relation_pis_psl += 3; labor_credibility += 4; household_policy_pressure += 3; barons_dissent -= 3; progressives_dissent += 5; last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession"; last_policy_authority = "PiS cabinet and Sejm majority"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Lewica trades its votes for recovery-fund safeguards"

Our votes pass the law and force Morawiecki to acknowledge social and local
safeguards he did not offer freely. PiS calls us responsible; KO calls us its
lifeline. Inside Lewica, the old parliamentary wing celebrates relevance while
progressives ask who will enforce a bargain owned by the cabinet.


- @poland_hub: Continue

@recovery_opposition
title: Demand one opposition amendment slate
subtitle: Requires working relations and compatible coalition instincts.
choose-if: ko_relation >= 45 and p2050_relation >= 28 and ko_coalition_openness >= 45 and p2050_coalition_openness >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: At least one opposition partner prefers a separate strategy.
on-arrival: recovery_fund_strategy = "Common opposition slate"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "A common opposition yes vote passes ratification with one control package"; ko_relation += 7; p2050_relation += 6; relation_ko_p2050 += 4; rival_relation_ko_p2050 += 4; pis_relation -= 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The opposition writes one recovery-fund control package and ratifies the law"

We arrive with KO and Poland 2050 at one list of controls and vote for the money
without giving Morawiecki a private partner. The opposition proves it can
govern a common interest; PiS tells voters that three rival parties needed a
week to say yes.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@recovery_abstain
title: Refuse a bilateral deal and abstain
on-arrival: recovery_fund_strategy = "Abstention"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1 if pis_seats + psl_seats >= 231; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "PiS and PSL provide the majority without Lewica" if recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "No alternative majority reaches 231" if recovery_fund_ratified = 0; pis_relation -= 2; ko_relation -= 3; p2050_relation -= 2; razem_dissent -= 2; public_trust -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 4; news_headline = "Lewica abstains and leaves ratification to the recorded PiS–PSL count"

[? if recovery_fund_ratified: PSL supplies the votes we withheld. The money
moves forward, PiS learns that another opposition partner is available, and we
own neither the safeguards nor the defeat of the government. ?]

[? if not recovery_fund_ratified: No alternative majority appears. The law
fails without our votes; Razem praises the refusal to rescue PiS while mayors
and unions ask why opposition discipline was worth delaying the fund. ?]

- @poland_hub: Continue


@recovery_palace
title: Ask Trzaskowski to sponsor and sign recovery-fund safeguards
subtitle: Cohabitation path: the President may convene, advocate and sign; Parliament and EU institutions still decide ratification and milestones.
view-if: trz_inaugurated = 1
choose-if: president_relation >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: The Palace will not guarantee a package without a working relationship.
on-arrival: recovery_fund_strategy = "Presidential sponsorship"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1 if pis_seats + ko_seats + p2050_seats + psl_seats >= 231; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "A Palace-convened cross-party majority ratifies; EU institutions retain milestone control"; president_relation += 7; ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 4; psl_relation += 3; pis_relation -= 5; judicial_legitimacy += 4; household_policy_pressure += 3; government_coalition_dissent += 7; trz_right_fragmentation += 10; trz_right_backlash += 5; rival_relation_pis_ko -= 4; last_policy_stage = "Presidential sponsorship"; last_policy_authority = "President may convene and sign; Sejm ratifies"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The President sponsors a recovery-fund control package for a Sejm vote"

We let President Trzaskowski convene the parties and sponsor the safeguards,
while the Sejm supplies the majority and EU institutions retain milestone
control. KO gains the photograph and we gain a package. Solidarna Polska attacks
both Morawiecki and the Palace, widening the governing fracture before the June
rights test.


- @poland_hub: Continue

@opposition_reset
# prose-audit: Grade B — The strategic choice now emerges from party competition and each route has a political aftermath; later trim any repeated opposition framing.
title: The opposition resets
new-page: true
on-arrival: opposition_reset_event_done = 1; news_headline = "KO and Poland 2050 contest the same centre"

= June 2021 — Three opposition strategies

KO asks every opposition party to line up behind a single anti-PiS pole.
Szymon Hołownia presents Poland 2050 as an escape from the habits of the old
opposition and courts voters who want a new centre. Our organisers hear both
pitches as an invitation to become somebody else's left flank.

The choice is not whether to oppose PiS. It is where we intend to remain
distinct while doing it.

- @reset_social
- @reset_democratic
- @reset_local

@reset_social
title: Compete with both on wages, housing and services
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "Social competition"; labor_credibility += 5; workers_support += 3; public_sector_support += 2; ko_relation -= 3; p2050_relation -= 3; left_economic_position -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica opens a social flank against both centrist parties"

Our MPs take wages, rents and public services on tour while KO and Poland 2050
compete over who can best manage the centre. Both accuse us of dividing the
opposition. Trade unionists and tenants' groups hear something rarer: a reason
to support the Left that is not merely fear of PiS.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@reset_democratic
title: Rebuild the democratic-opposition table
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "Democratic opposition table"; resources -= 1; ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 5; relation_ko_p2050 += 4; rival_relation_ko_p2050 += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; razem_dissent += 3; news_headline = "The opposition table returns with written limits"

Lawyers and parliamentary whips sit down to agree on constitutional red lines,
procedural warnings and the votes on which nobody will surprise the others.
The table gives the opposition discipline without pretending it has one
programme. Razem still fears that every shared photograph teaches voters to
see us as a junior partner in somebody else's coalition.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@reset_local
title: Leave Warsaw to the leaders and organise counties
on-arrival: opposition_reset_strategy = "County organisation"; local_network += 5; rural_support += 3; psl_relation += 3; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "County organisation replaces another leaders' summit"

The next Warsaw summit takes place without us. Our money goes instead to county
offices, bus-stop meetings and organisers looking for credible local
candidates. It produces fewer evening headlines, but more people know whom to
call when a clinic closes. PSL notices that the Left has begun treating the
counties as political ground rather than scenery between cities.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@left_revolt
title: The merger revolt
new-page: true
go-to: left_revolt_skipped if nowa_lewica_merger_agreed = 0; left_revolt_live if nowa_lewica_merger_agreed = 1

@left_revolt_skipped
title: No merger revolt
new-page: true
on-arrival: left_revolt_event_done = 1; merger_revolt_leader = "No merger"; merger_resolution = "No merger, no revolt"; news_headline = "Without a merger, there is no merger leadership to revolt against"
go-to: poland_hub

@left_revolt_live
# prose-audit: Grade B — Conditional leadership stakes and six distinct aftermaths now carry the scene; preserve this branch sensitivity in later edits.
title: The merger revolt
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_revolt_event_done = 1;
const selectedLeader = String(Q.merger_leader || "");
const razemHasBureauSeat =
    Q.zandberg_advisor || Q.biejat_advisor ||
    Q.zawisza_advisor || Q.matysiak_advisor;
if (
    selectedLeader == "Razem" &&
    Q.razem_merged &&
    razemHasBureauSeat
) {
    Q.merger_revolt_leader = "Razem";
} else if (
    selectedLeader == "Włodzimierz Czarzasty" &&
    Q.czarzasty_advisor
) {
    Q.merger_revolt_leader = "Włodzimierz Czarzasty";
} else if (selectedLeader == "Dual chairs") {
    Q.merger_revolt_leader =
        Q.czarzasty_advisor && Q.barons_strength >= Q.spring_strength
            ? "Włodzimierz Czarzasty"
            : (Q.biedron_advisor ? "Dual chairs" : "Members");
} else {
    Q.merger_revolt_leader = "Members";
}
Q.news_headline = Q.merger_revolt_leader == "Razem"
    ? "The old apparatus revolts against Razem's merger leadership"
    : (Q.merger_revolt_leader == "Włodzimierz Czarzasty"
        ? "Nowa Lewica's merger dispute becomes a parliamentary revolt"
        : "The merger's unresolved leadership produces a parliamentary revolt");
!}

= July 2021 — The merger revolt

The new party has a name, statutes and two sets of people who believe they were
promised control. Parliamentary offices, regional lists and access to the
membership register turn an argument about principle into an argument about
keys.

[? if merger_revolt_leader = "Włodzimierz Czarzasty": Internal opponents now
challenge Czarzasty's control of the merger. We must decide whether authority
remains with the executive or moves toward a broader, member-led Left.?]
[? if merger_revolt_leader = "Razem": SLD organisers and displaced Wiosna
figures challenge the settlement we placed under Razem. It can enforce the
mandate it won, guarantee the defeated currents a place or submit its
leadership to the membership again.?]
[? if merger_revolt_leader = "Dual chairs": Neither protected chair can
command the merged organisation alone. We must decide whether parity survives,
the apparatus takes control or members arbitrate.?]
[? if merger_revolt_leader = "Members": Members or a constituent convention
were entrusted with the merger, but the old organisations still control
offices and nominations. We are about to learn whether our rules can govern
the machine.?]

- @revolt_suspend
- @revolt_mediate
- @revolt_ballot
- @revolt_razem_enforce
- @revolt_razem_pact
- @revolt_razem_ballot

@revolt_suspend
title: Suspend the internal opponents
view-if: merger_revolt_leader != "Razem"
on-arrival: merger_resolution = "Executive suspensions"; barons_dissent -= 8; barons_strength += 3; party_unity -= 10; progressives_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 6; public_trust -= 4; news_headline = "The executive suspends its internal opponents"

Suspension letters reach the rebels before the next parliamentary meeting.
They lose committee posts, office access and the right to speak in the party's
name; the executive briefs that discipline has been restored. Regional chairs
understand the warning. The public sees a purge, and inside the party unity now
means that the losing side has been made silent.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@revolt_mediate
title: Ask the five currents for a binding truce
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
view-if: merger_revolt_leader != "Razem"
choose-if: resources >= 1 and faction_vetoes <= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource and no multi-caucus veto.
on-arrival: merger_resolution = "Five-current truce"; resources -= 1; party_unity += 6; barons_dissent -= 3; spring_dissent -= 3; labor_dissent -= 3; progressives_dissent -= 3; razem_dissent -= 3; news_headline = "A binding truce postpones the purge"

Delegates from all five currents spend a day behind a closed door dividing
nominations, appeal rights and the limits of public dissent. Nobody receives
the whole party; everybody receives enough protection to return to work. The
truce ends the immediate revolt without settling its cause, and each current
keeps a copy for the next dispute.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@revolt_ballot
title: Put the merger leadership to a member ballot
view-if: merger_revolt_leader != "Razem"
on-arrival: merger_resolution = "Membership ballot"; party_unity += 3; public_trust += 3; barons_dissent += 7; progressives_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 3; organiser_energy += 2; news_headline = "Members decide who controls the merger"

The membership register is opened and branch meetings replace disciplinary
hearings. Office-holders who expected to settle the merger among themselves
must campaign for authority in public view. The ballot gives the eventual
winner a mandate, but it also gives every unresolved grievance several weeks
at a microphone.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@revolt_razem_enforce
title: Enforce Razem's constituent mandate
subtitle: Razem keeps command; the old apparatus treats discipline as a purge.
view-if: merger_revolt_leader = "Razem"
on-arrival: merger_resolution = "Razem discipline"; razem_dissent -= 8; razem_strength += 3; party_unity -= 10; barons_dissent += 12; spring_dissent += 7; public_trust -= 3; news_headline = "Razem disciplines the apparatus rebellion"

Razem answers the rebellion with the constituent mandate and a stack of
disciplinary letters. Its command is formally intact, but veteran SLD networks
slow appointments and displaced Wiosna organisers stop lending their names to
the project. We have defended the rules under which Razem took charge while
making the organisation beneath that command harder to move.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@revolt_razem_pact
title: Guarantee every defeated current a place
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Razem leads, but appointments and nominations become plural.
view-if: merger_revolt_leader = "Razem"
choose-if: resources >= 1 and faction_vetoes <= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource and no multi-caucus veto.
on-arrival: merger_resolution = "Razem-led current pact"; resources -= 1; party_unity += 7; razem_dissent -= 4; barons_dissent -= 6; spring_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 3; progressives_dissent -= 3; news_headline = "Razem secures its lead by protecting every internal current"

Razem keeps the chair, but appointments, nominations and appeal panels are
shared among the currents. The defeated organisations stop boycotting the new
structure because each can point to a place inside it. Our leadership becomes
slower and less tidy; it also becomes something the whole party may consent to
obey.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@revolt_razem_ballot
title: Put Razem's leadership back to the full membership
view-if: merger_revolt_leader = "Razem"
on-arrival: merger_resolution = "Membership ballot"; party_unity += 3; public_trust += 3; razem_dissent += 7; barons_dissent -= 5; organiser_energy += 2; news_headline = "Members decide whether Razem keeps the merger leadership"

Razem puts a mandate it already won at risk and asks the full membership to
confirm it. Its activists resent being made to fight the same battle twice;
the old apparatus can no longer claim it was denied a contest. Whatever the
result, control of the merger will come from counted members rather than keys
to inherited offices.

- @poland_hub: Continue
